   "source": [
    "# Milestone 4 – Incident Type Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4e23c741",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Objective:\n",
    "To analyze disaster data to identify patterns, trends, and impacts across time, location, and incident types."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6770545c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Step 1: Dataset Preparation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "204d8763",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Disaster Type : Present\n",
      "State : Present\n",
      "Year : Present\n",
      "Month : Present\n",
      "Individuals & Households Program : Present\n",
      "Public Assistance Program : Present\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "required_cols = ['Disaster Type', 'State', 'Year', 'Month',\n",
    "                 'Individuals & Households Program',\n",
    "                 'Public Assistance Program']\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in required_cols:\n",
    "    print(col, \":\", \"Present\" if col in df.columns else \"Missing\")\n",
    "df.rename(columns={\n",
    "    'Disaster Type': 'incidentType',\n",
    "    'State': 'state',\n",
    "    'Year': 'year',\n",
    "    'Month': 'month',\n",
    "    'Individuals & Households Program': 'ihProgramDeclared',\n",
    "    'Public Assistance Program': 'paProgramDeclared'\n",
    "}, inplace=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f72dc33",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Step 2: Incident Type Distribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "10466653",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "incident_counts = df['incidentType'].value_counts()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n",
    "incident_counts.plot(kind='bar')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Distribution of Disaster Types\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Incident Type\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "plt.grid(axis='y')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "22ecae57",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "1.The chart shows the frequency of each disaster type across the dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "2.Storms, floods, and hurricanes are among the most frequent disaster categories.\n",
    "\n",
    "3.Rare events like tsunamis or volcanic activities occur very infrequently.\n",
    "\n",
    "The distribution indicates that weather-related disasters dominate overall disaster occurrences."
   ]
  },
