    "Confirms skewed distribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7cf7d7ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Step 3: State vs Incident Type (Heatmap)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "eb335ced",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1400x800 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "heatmap_data = df.groupby(['state', 'incidentType']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14,8))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(heatmap_data, cmap='Reds')\n",
    "plt.title(\"State vs Incident Type Heatmap\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Incident Type\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"State\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "db1da8a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Interpretation\n",
    "1.The heatmap highlights disaster intensity across states and incident types.\n",
    "\n",
    "2.Some states show strong dominance of specific disasters (e.g., hurricanes or floods).\n",
    "\n",
    "3.High-density areas indicate disaster-prone regions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The heatmap reveals strong regional specialization in disaster types."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99573725",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Step 4: Disaster Assistance Program Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "752e0c28",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "assistance_analysis = df.groupby('incidentType')[[\n",
    "    'ihProgramDeclared',\n",
    "    'paProgramDeclared'\n",
    "]].apply(lambda x: (x == 'Yes').sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "assistance_analysis.plot(kind='bar', figsize=(12,6))\n",
    "plt.title(\"Disaster Type vs Assistance Programs\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Incident Type\")\n",
